hadiths[91]{hadithnumber,text}:
"661","Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Ibn Tawus said to me that my father has a book in which the mention of those blood monies (diyah) is found upon which revelation was sent down. And whatever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made obligatory regarding blood monies and zakat, revelation was sent down about it."
"662","It is narrated from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) that he possesses a book regarding blood money (diyah) upon which revelation was sent down. And whatever charity the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory or whatever blood money he made obligatory, revelation was sent down regarding it. And it has been said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never performed any action without Allah’s revelation; one type of revelation is that which is recited, and the other is the revelation that was sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he acted upon it."
"663","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made obligatory the Sadaqat al-Fitr of one sa’ of dates or one sa’ of barley upon every free person, slave, male, and female among the Muslims."
"664","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Zakat al-Fitr obligatory on every free person, slave, man, and woman among those whom you support."
"665","Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we used to give one sa’ of food, or one sa’ of barley, or one sa’ of dates, or one sa’ of raisins as zakat al-fitr."
"666","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made obligatory the Zakat al-Fitr upon the people as one sa’ of dates or one sa’ of barley."
"667","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we used to give the Zakat of Fitr (Sadaqat al-Fitr) as one sa’ of food, or one sa’ of barley, or one sa’ of dates, or one sa’ of raisins, or one sa’ of cheese."
"668","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, we used to give one sa' of food, or one sa' of raisins, or one sa' of cheese, or one sa' of dates, or one sa' of barley as zakat al-fitr. We continued to give this until Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) came for Hajj or 'Umrah, delivered a sermon to the people, and among what he said to them was: ""In my opinion, two mudd of wheat from Syria are equal to one sa' of dates."" Then the people adopted this method."
"669","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give dates as Sadaqat al-Fitr, except on one occasion when he gave barley."
"670","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we used to give one sa’ of food, one sa’ of barley, one sa’ of dates, one sa’ of raisins, and one sa’ of cheese as Sadaqat al-Fitr."
"671","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to send the Sadaqat al-Fitr to the collector one or two days before Eid al-Fitr."
"672","With this same chain, it is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that they used to send the Sadaqat al-Fitr to the collector one or two days before."
"673","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent Muadh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) to (Yemen), he said to him: ""If they accept this, then inform them that there is charity (zakat) due upon them, which is to be taken from their wealthy and returned to their needy."""
"674","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I ask you by Allah, has Allah commanded you to take charity from our wealthy and return it to our needy?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: ""Allah is witness (yes, it is so)."""
"675","Qabeesah bin Mukhaariq al-Hilaali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I took on a guarantee. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, so the Prophet ﷺ said: ""We will fulfill it."""
"676","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Adi bin Khiyar (may Allah be pleased with him) that two men informed him that both of them came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him for charity. The Prophet (ﷺ) looked at them from head to toe and said: ""If you wish (I will give you), but there is no share in charity for a wealthy person nor for one who is strong and able to earn."""
"677","It is narrated from Usama bin Zaid Al-Laithi, may Allah have mercy on him, that he asked Salim bin Abdullah, may Allah have mercy on him, about Zakat. He said: ""You should give it yourself."" Usama says: ""I said, did not Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say that it should be delivered to the ruler?"" He said: ""Yes. But in my opinion, it is not necessary to deliver it to the ruler."""
"678","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding those who refused to pay zakat: ""Did not the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say, 'I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: ﴿La ilaha illallah﴾. When they say it, their blood and wealth will be protected from me except for its due right (i.e., legal retribution, etc.), and their reckoning is with Allah'?"" Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""Is not zakat its due right, which they have refused to give?"""
"679","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say 'There is no god but Allah,' their lives and property become protected from me, except for its due right (i.e., in cases such as retribution, etc.), and their reckoning is with Allah."" Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This is included in its due right. If they withhold even a rope used for tying a camel, which they used to give to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I will fight them for it."
"680","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said this or something similar in meaning to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"681","Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever does not give the zakat of his wealth, on the Day of Resurrection his wealth will be turned into a bald serpent. The man will run from it, and it will chase him until it is made to encircle his neck like a collar.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited this verse to us: “Soon, on the Day of Resurrection, those things they withheld out of miserliness will be made into collars around their necks.” (Aal-e-Imran: 180)"
"682","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Whoever possesses wealth and does not pay its zakat, then on the Day of Resurrection his wealth will be turned into a bald snake, which will have two spots over its eyes. It will search for him until it finds him and will say, ""I am your treasure."""
"683","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Whoever possesses wealth and does not pay its zakat, then on the Day of Resurrection his wealth will be turned into a bald snake with two spots over its eyes. It will seek him out until it finds him and will say, ""I am your treasure."""
"684","Abdullah bin Dinar says: I heard Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) being asked about ""Kanz"" (hoarded wealth), so he replied: It is that wealth on which you do not pay Zakat."
"685","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: Every wealth from which you pay zakat is not a treasure, even if it is buried, and every wealth from which you do not pay zakat is a treasure, even if it is not buried."
"686","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports: I heard Abul Qasim ﷺ saying, ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! Whoever gives charity from lawful earnings—and Allah accepts only what is lawful—and only charity from lawful earnings reaches Allah. It is as if someone places it in the hand of the Most Merciful, then He (Allah) increases it for the giver, just as one of you raises his young animal by feeding and nurturing it, until a single morsel becomes as great as a huge mountain on the Day of Resurrection."" Then the Prophet ﷺ recited this verse: ""Allah is the One Who accepts repentance from His servants and accepts charities."" (__QUR_N__ at-Tawbah: 104)"
"687","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The example of the one who gives charity and the miser is like two persons wearing two coats of mail or armors from their chests up to their collarbones. When the generous person intends to spend, the armor covers his body or extends over him until it covers his clothes, and its traces disappear as he walks. But when the miser intends to spend, the coat tightens, and every ring clings to its place, until it even squeezes his neck or throat. The miser tries to loosen it, but he cannot loosen it."""
"688","Through another chain, it is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in a similar manner, but in it the words are: ""that he tries to widen it, but is not able to do so."""
"689","Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When the collector of Zakat comes to you, he should leave you pleased."""
"690","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban narrates that two men from the Ashja‘ tribe told him that Muhammad bin Maslamah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) used to come to them to collect zakat, and he would say to the owner of the wealth: ""Bring the zakat property."" Whenever a goat, for which it was necessary to fulfill the due right, was brought, he would accept it."
"691","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""Zakat is not obligatory on wealth until a year has passed over it."""
"692","It is narrated from Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) that Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""This is the month of your zakat; whoever has a debt should pay it off so that only your pure wealth remains, then pay zakat from that."""
"693","Qudamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When I used to come to Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) to receive my salary, he would ask me: ""Is zakat obligatory on the wealth you possess?"" If I said yes, he would deduct zakat from my salary, and if I said no, he would give me my salary."
"694","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: “This is the charity (the prescribed amount for zakat), then goats and some other things were exempted, and people disliked this.” This is the obligation of zakat which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made obligatory upon the Muslims, and Allah Almighty commanded him regarding it. Therefore, whoever asks the believers for zakat according to this, they should give it, and if anyone asks for more than this, they must not give it. For twenty-four or fewer camels, for every five, one goat must be given. If the number of camels reaches twenty-five, then from twenty-five to thirty-five, a one-year-old female camel (bint makhad) is obligatory; if there is no one-year-old female camel, then a two-year-old male camel (ibn labun), which has entered its third year, is obligatory. When the number of camels reaches thirty-six, then from thirty-six to forty-five, a two-year-old female camel (bint labun) is obligatory. When the number reaches forty-six, then from forty-six to sixty, a three-year-old she-camel capable of mating (hiqqah) is obligatory. And when the number reaches sixty-one, then from sixty-one to seventy-five, a four-year-old female camel (jadh’ah) is obligatory. When the number reaches seventy-six, then from seventy-six to ninety, two-year-old female camels (two bint labun) are obligatory. When the number reaches ninety-one, then from ninety-one to one hundred and twenty, two she-camels capable of mating (two hiqqah) are obligatory, and when the number exceeds one hundred and twenty, then for every forty, a two-year-old female camel, and for every fifty, a three-year-old female camel is obligatory. If the ages of the camels for the obligatory charity are different, then if someone’s camels reach the number for which a jadh’ah is obligatory, but he does not have a jadh’ah, rather he has a hiqqah, then along with the hiqqah, two goats should also be taken from him as zakat, if it is easy for him to give them, otherwise twenty dirhams should be taken. And if someone is obliged to give a hiqqah in zakat, but he does not have a hiqqah, rather he has a jadh’ah, then the jadh’ah should be taken from him, and the zakat collector should give twenty dirhams or two goats to the one giving zakat."
"695","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a hadith with the same meaning (as the previous hadith), but I remember from it that: ""The one who gives zakat will not give two goats or 20 dirhams. I do not remember whether this applies if it is easy for him to give them."" And I think that in the hadith narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) through the chain of Hammad, he said that Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) gave me the book of charity transmitted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then he mentioned the same meaning as I have stated."
"696","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that this is the book of alms (its details), and in it is that for every twenty-four or fewer camels, one goat is due, and for every five, one goat, and above that up to thirty-five, a one-year-old she-camel is obligatory. If there is no one-year-old she-camel, then a two-year-old male camel that has entered its third year is to be given, and above that up to forty-five, a two-year-old she-camel that has entered its third year is due. And above that up to sixty, a three-year-old she-camel that is capable of mating is due. And above that up to seventy-five, a four-year-old she-camel is due. And above that up to ninety, two-year-old she-camels are due. And above that up to one hundred and twenty, two three-year-old she-camels that are capable of mating are due. And when the number exceeds this, then for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel, and for every fifty, a three-year-old she-camel is obligatory. And the zakat of goats that graze (in the wild or open fields, etc.) is as follows: when their number is from forty to one hundred and twenty, one goat is obligatory. Above that up to two hundred, two goats, and above that up to three hundred, three goats are obligatory, and when the number exceeds this, then for every hundred, one goat is obligatory. And in zakat, an old, defective, or male (goat) should not be given unless the collector of alms deems it appropriate and accepts it. And due to fear of (increased) zakat, wealth should not be combined when separate, nor separated when combined. And when there are two partners, they should calculate their shares equally, and when silver reaches five awqiyah, then one-fortieth (two and a half percent) zakat is obligatory. This is the wording of the copy of Umar bin Khattab’s (may Allah be pleased with him) book according to which he used to collect zakat from people. Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “We will take all of this (i.e., this is our school of thought).”"
"697","Salim bin Abdullah narrates from his father, and he from the Prophet ﷺ. I do not know whether in the narration through Sufyan bin Husain, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) or not. Regarding the zakat of camels, it is narrated in the same meanings which are not contrary to this, and I do not know, rather if Allah wills, I have no doubt except that he narrated to me the entire hadith regarding goats, partners among themselves, and silver in the same way, except that I was only able to remember the part about camels from his narration."
"698","Bashar bin Asim narrates from his father that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed Abu Sufyan bin Abdullah as the collector (of zakat) in Ta’if and its surrounding areas. When he went out to collect charity (zakat), he counted the young animals (offspring) along with the adults. While they did not take zakat from those young ones, the people said: “If you are counting these young ones, then you should also take them from us as zakat.” He refrained (from collecting zakat) until he came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said to him: “Be aware that these people think that you are counting their young animals but by not taking zakat from them, you are being unjust to them.” So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: “Count their young animals as well, even the one (so small) that the shepherd carries in his hand, and say to them: I will not take from you a suckling animal, nor one close to giving birth, nor a milking animal, nor a fattened animal for slaughter, nor a billy goat used for mating with the goats. And take from them an ‘anaq, a jadh’ah, and a two-year-old animal, and this is of average quality between the bad and the good.”"
"699","It is narrated from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that two men came to me and said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has sent us so that we may collect zakat from the people."" Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I brought out for them a pregnant goat, which was the best among my goats, but they refused to take it and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has forbidden us from taking a pregnant goat (as zakat)."" Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""I then gave them a goat of average quality, and they accepted it."""
"700","The noble wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates that when the zakat goats were passing by Umar ibn Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), he saw among them a goat whose udder was full of milk. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""What about this goat?"" The people said, ""It is one of the goats given in charity."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Its owners must not have given it willingly. Do not put people to trial, do not take the best of the Muslims’ wealth, and refrain from taking their food (milk-giving animals)."""
"701","It is narrated from Tawoos Yamani (may Allah have mercy on him) that Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) took a one-year-old calf (which had entered the second year) from thirty cows, and for every forty, he took a two-year-old calf. When he was given one of lesser age, he refused to take it and said: ""I have not heard anything about this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ); (I will not take it) until I ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about it."" Tawoos says that before Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) could come (to Madinah), the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed away."
"702","It is narrated from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) that cows less than the nisab of zakat were brought to Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) did not command me anything regarding this."""
"703","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no zakat on less than five camels."""
"704","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat on less than five camels."""
"705","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no zakat in less than five camels."""
"706","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakat is not obligatory on a Muslim for his slave and his horse."""
"707","From another chain of narration, it is reported from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet ﷺ in a manner similar to the previous hadith."
"708","Iraq bin Malik narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) in the same way as a mawquf narration."
"709","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) who says: I asked Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) about the zakat on non-Arab horses, so he said: ""Is zakat obligatory on horses?"""
"710","It is narrated from Abu Amr bin Hamaas, from his father, who said: I passed by Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) while I was carrying leather on my neck. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do you not pay the zakat on your wealth, O Hamaas?"" Hamaas says: I said, ""I have nothing except this bag of collected leather which is on my back."" He said: ""This is wealth, put it down."" Hamaas says: I placed it before him, he calculated it and found that zakat was due on it, then he took zakat from it."
"711","Abu Amr bin Hamaas narrates from his father in a similar manner through another chain of narration."
"712","It is narrated from Zuraiq bin Hakeem that Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, wrote to him (a letter) stating that whatever merchandise of the Muslims passes by you, take zakat from their trade goods. For every forty dinars, take one dinar. If it is less than that, then take zakat in proportion, up to twenty dinars. If it is less by a third of a dinar, then leave it and do not take zakat from that amount."
"713","It is narrated from Yusuf bin Mahak (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Invest the wealth of the orphan in trade, lest zakat consumes and finishes it."""
"714","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrates from his father that he said: The wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), used to take care of me and my two brothers who were orphans, and she used to give zakat from our wealth."
"715","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrates from his father that he said: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to raise me and my brother, and she would give zakat from our wealth."
"716","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to give zakat from the wealth of the orphan."
"717","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar that Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Invest the wealth of orphans in trade, lest zakat consumes it."
"718","It is narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad who says that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to give zakat from our wealth and trade was conducted with it in Bahrain."
"719","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: There is no zakat on wealth until there is an intention of trade."
"720","It is narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the orphaned daughters of her brother were under her care and they also had jewelry, but she did not take out zakat from it."
"721","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to adorn her brother's daughters with gold jewelry and did not pay zakat on it."
"722","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that his daughters and young girls used to have gold (in the form of jewelry) and he did not take out zakat from it."
"723","Amr bin Dinar narrates that I heard a man asking Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Is there zakat on jewelry?"" He replied, ""No."" The man said, ""Even if (the jewelry) reaches one thousand dinars?"" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""Even if it is more than that, still no."""
"724","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakat is not obligatory on silver less than five awqiyah."""
"725","Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat on less than five awqiyah."""
"726","This hadith is also narrated in the same manner through another chain of transmission."
"727","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And there is a fifth (share) in the buried treasure."""
"728","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is a fifth (share) in buried treasure (Rikaz)."""
"729","It is narrated from Ibn Musayyib and Abu Salamah that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""There is a fifth (share) in the buried treasure (Dafeenah)."""
"730","Amr bin Shu'aib narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said regarding the treasure which a man found in a deserted land of the pre-Islamic period: ""And if you found it in a populated town or on a public road, then announce it, and if you found it in a deserted place of the pre-Islamic period or an uninhabited settlement, then there is a fifth in it and in buried treasure."""
"731","It is narrated from Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) who states that a man came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I have found fifteen hundred dirhams in an uninhabited place in the region of Sawad. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will give a very clear ruling on this. If you found it in such an uninhabited place that is adjacent to another settlement, then this money belongs to the people of that settlement. And if you found it in such a settlement whose uninhabited area is not adjacent to another, then four-fifths are for you and one-fifth is for us, then another fifth is for you."
"732","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And in buried treasure (Dafeenah) there is a fifth (as zakat)."""
"733","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked about ambergris, so he said: If there is anything in it, then it is the fifth part."
"734","It is narrated from Tawus that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about ambergris, so he said: If there is anything in it, then it is the fifth part."
"735","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There is no zakat on ambergris; it is merely a thing that the sea throws onto the shore."
"736","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: There is nothing (prohibited) in ambergris; it is just a thing that the sea throws up on the shore."
"737","It is narrated from ‘Itab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding the zakat of grapes: “Its estimation will be made just as the estimation is made for date palms. Then its zakat will be given in raisins just as the zakat of date palms is given in dates.”"
"738","It is from this previous chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to send people to the people who would estimate their grapes and fruits."
"739","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: The charity (zakat) of fruits and crops—whether dates, grapes, crops, barley, or sult (a type of barley grown in Hijaz that resembles wheat)—which derive moisture from the earth, or are irrigated by a canal, or watered by a spring, or irrigated by rain, in these there is a tenth (one-tenth) due. For every ten, one part will be taken. And for that which is irrigated by drawing water with buckets or by bringing water with animals, there is half of a tenth (one-twentieth) due; for every twenty, one part will be taken. For the field irrigated by drawing water with buckets or by bringing water with animals, one-twentieth (of the produce) will be taken."
"740","Sa’d bin Abi Dhibab narrates that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and accepted Islam. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah! Due to my people accepting Islam, appoint someone to collect zakat from their wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did so and appointed me as their collector. Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also appointed me as a collector, and then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did the same. The narrator says that Sa’d was among the respected ones. Sa’d says: I spoke to my people about honey and told them: There is zakat in it, because wealth from which zakat is not given has no blessing in it. They asked: How much is it? Sa’d says: I said: One-tenth. Sa’d says: I took one-tenth from them and brought it to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted it, sold it, and deposited its price among the charities of the Muslims."
"741","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to take one-twentieth from wheat and oil that was irrigated by water being drawn out. He intended by this that goods should be brought in abundance to Madinah, and from pulses he used to take one-tenth (ushr)."
"742","Saib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the time of Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), I was an official in the market of Madinah along with Abdullah bin Utbah. Abdullah bin Utbah used to collect ‘ushr (a type of tax) from the Nabateans."
"743","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat on dates less than five wasqs."""
"744","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat on produce less than five wasq."""
"745","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakat on produce less than five wasq."""
"746","Abu Humayd Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed a man from the tribe of Asad, whose name was Ibn al-Lubtiyyah, as a collector of charity. When he returned, he said: This is your wealth, and this was given to me as a gift. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood on the pulpit and said: “What is the matter with an agent whom we send for some of our tasks, and he comes and says: This is your (public) wealth and this was given to me as a gift? Why did he not sit in the house of his father or mother and see whether he would be given gifts there or not? By Him in Whose hand is my soul, whoever takes anything unlawfully from this (charity) will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on his neck. If it is a camel, it will be groaning; if it is a cow, it will be mooing; and if it is a goat, it will be bleating.” Then he raised his blessed hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits and said: “O Allah! Have I conveyed Your command? O Allah! Have I conveyed Your command?”"
"747","It is narrated from Abu Humaid Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that my eyes saw and my ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and you may ask Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), that is, in the same manner as the previous hadith."
"748","It is narrated from Tawoos, may Allah have mercy on him, that he states: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, appointed Ubadah bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, as a collector of charity, and said: ""O Abu al-Waleed! Fear Allah! Lest you come on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on your neck, and it is groaning, or a cow that is mooing, or a goat that is bleating."" Ubadah bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it really like that? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Yes, by Him in Whose hand is my soul, except for the one upon whom Allah has mercy."" Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Him Who has sent you with the truth, I will never again become an agent over even two things."
"749","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity that is mixed with wealth destroys it."""
"750","It is narrated from Aslam (may Allah have mercy on him), he reports that he said to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): Among these camels, there is a blind she-camel. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Is it among the animals of jizya (tax) or among the animals of sadaqah (zakat)? Aslam said: It is among the animals of jizya (tax). He said: It bears the mark of jizya."
"751","The freed slave of Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was with Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), during the summer days, with his wealth in the nearby settlements of Madinah, when he saw a man driving two young camels and walking on the ground like moths due to the intensity of the heat. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What is with this man, why did he not stay in Madinah until it became cooler, then travel? When the man came closer, he said: Look, who is this? I said, a man covering himself with a sheet, driving the young camels. When the man came even closer, he said again: Look! I looked and it was Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). I said, this is the Commander of the Faithful. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and put his head out of the door, but the heat of the wind hurt him, so he pulled his head back in until Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came near. He asked: Why have you come out at this time? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Two young camels of the charity camels were left behind while the charity camels had already gone ahead. I wanted to bring them to the pasture to join the others. I feared they might get lost and then Allah would question me about them. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Commander of the Faithful! Come to our water and shade (meaning, drink water and rest in the shade). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: You stay in your shade. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We have what you need. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: You stay in your shade. Then he went on. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever wishes to see a trustworthy, strong man, let him look at him. Then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) returned to us (in the shade) and became absorbed in thought."
